    "text": "By Staff Report ,\n17 hours ago CHAMBERSBURG- Pennsylvania State Police are investigating a reported theft from the Walmart on Conestoga Drive in Shippensburg Township, Cumberland County this fall. Troopers say that someone stole a towel set ($13.97 value), a bathmat ($11.44 value), and a memo book ($0.04 value) from the retailer around 12:38pm on October 22nd. That person, who’s description has not been released, left in a silver or aluminum colored Ford Fusion. PSP continue to investigate. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 11",
